{
  "tema": 6755,
  "slug": "el-siete-numeros-masculinos",
  "titulo": "Numbers are masculine",
  "subtitulo": "El siete es mi número de la suerte.",
  "foto": "t05.jpg",
  "regla": "When you talk about a number itself (the figure, a grade, a lucky number), it is a masculine noun: el siete, un diez, los ochos.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "A number used as a **noun** (the figure itself) is **masculine**: **el cinco**, **un siete**, **el cero**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It's masculine because it stands for **el número**: **el siete** = **el número siete**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Plural adds **-s** (or **-es**): **los sietes**, **dos ochos**, **tres seises**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Careful: in **la 15** (a room, a bus route), the article goes with the hidden feminine noun: **la (habitación) 15**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==El siete== es mi número de la suerte.",
              "en": "Seven is my lucky number."
            },
            {
              "es": "Saqué ==un diez== en el examen.",
              "en": "I got a ten on the test."
            },
            {
              "es": "Tu cinco parece ==un seis==.",
              "en": "Your five looks like a six."
            },
